      Formatted Input: Which feature does not form as a result of tectonic plates diverging?
A. trench
B. rift valley
C. ocean basin
D. mid-ocean ridge
        Answer:            **B. trench**

Trenches do not form due to tectonic plates diverging. Instead, they are associated with convergent processes where one plate is forced beneath another. This process of subduction can lead to the formation of deep trenches as seen along certain coastlines and oceanic ridges. In contrast, ocean basins, rift valleys, and mid-ocean ridges all form due to the movement apart of tectonic plates.
